    {
      "id": "jshell-301-filter-map",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "source": "//@ anchor: filter-and-map-the-workhorses\n//@ description: filter and map - the workhorses\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.stream.Collectors;\n\n// --- filter and map - the workhorses ---\n// filter(Predicate) decides which elements continue: it changes HOW MANY.\n// map(Function)     replaces each element with something else: it changes WHAT.\n\nList<String> words = List.of(\"banana\", \"apple\", \"cherry\", \"blueberry\",\n                              \"apricot\", \"avocado\", \"kiwi\", \"blackberry\");\n\n// The lambda w -> w.startsWith(\"b\") is a Predicate: one element in, boolean out.\n// Nothing runs until collect() - the terminal operation - asks for the results.\nList<String> bWords = words.stream()\n    .filter(w -> w.startsWith(\"b\"))\n    .collect(Collectors.toList());       // gather what survived into a new List\nSystem.out.println(\"Words starting with 'b': \" + bWords);\n\n// map turns Stream<String> into Stream<Integer> - the element type changes.\nList<Integer> lengths = words.stream()\n    .map(String::length)                // method reference: same as w -> w.length()\n    .collect(Collectors.toList());\nSystem.out.println(\"Word lengths           : \" + lengths);\n\n// Operations compose, and ORDER MATTERS for cost: filtering first means the map and\n// the sort only handle the elements that survived.\nList<String> result = words.stream()\n    .filter(w -> w.length() > 5)        // keep the long ones\n    .map(String::toUpperCase)           // then uppercase only those\n    .sorted()                           // natural (alphabetical) order\n    .collect(Collectors.toList());\nSystem.out.println(\"Long words (uppercase, sorted): \" + result);\n\n// mapToInt drops down to an IntStream, which is where average()/sum()/max() live.\n// average() returns an OptionalDouble because an empty stream has no average -\n// orElse supplies the fallback rather than letting a null escape.\ndouble avgLength = words.stream()\n    .mapToInt(String::length)\n    .average()\n    .orElse(0.0);\nSystem.out.printf(\"Average word length: %.2f%n\", avgLength);",
      "output": "",
      "returnValue": null,
      "executed": false,
      "executionCount": null,
      "error": "",
      "anchor": "filter-and-map-the-workhorses",
      "dependsOn": [],
